{"id": "xgreece", "name": "Vikos-Aoös National Park", "short": "Vikos-Aoös", "place": "Epirus, Greece", "lat": 39.95, "lon": 20.7, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Greece", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Gorge cliffs, oak woods, chamois, wolves and brown bears in the Pindus.", "tip": {"id": "wolf", "title": "Remove the wolf", "text": "Set Gray wolf to -100% and watch chamois, roe deer and wild boar numbers rise, then pressure on oaks and mountain grasses, and less carrion for ravens."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Vikos-Aoös National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vikos%E2%80%93Ao%C3%B6s_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Vikos Gorge", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vikos_Gorge"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Balkan chamois", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balkan_chamois"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Brown bear", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_bear"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Vikos Gorge", "icon": "grizzly", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "oak", "sp": "quercus", "xh": 0.1, "name": "Kermes oak & oaks", "desc": "Oaks, including kermes oak recorded near the site, are common in the sub-Mediterranean woodland and drop acorns that many animals eat.", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "hornbeam", "sp": "ostrya carpinifolia", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "festuca", "sp": "festuca", "xh": 0.55, "name": "Mountain grasslands", "desc": "Grasses of the subalpine meadows above about 1,500 m, where chamois graze in summer."}, {"id": "sideritis", "sp": "sideritis", "xh": 0.8}, {"id": "chamois", "sp": "rupicapra rupicapra", "xh": 0.05, "name": "Balkan chamois", "desc": "A rare goat-antelope of the gorge cliffs. It eats highland grasses and herbs in summer and moves lower in winter.", "badge": "Keystone grazer"}, {"id": "roedeer", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.2, "desc": "A small woodland deer that browses leaves, shoots and herbs. It is recorded in the area."}, {"id": "boar", "sp": "sus scrofa", "xh": 0.36, "desc": "An omnivore that roots for acorns, plants and invertebrates in the woods."}, {"id": "mouse", "sp": "apodemus sylvaticus", "xh": 0.52}, {"id": "dormouse", "sp": "glis glis", "xh": 0.68, "desc": "A tree-climbing rodent that eats nuts, seeds and fruit and is prey of foxes and martens."}, {"id": "jay", "sp": "garrulus glandarius", "xh": 0.86, "desc": "A woodland crow well known for gathering and caching acorns."}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.1, "wiki": "Red fox", "desc": "A versatile hunter of small mammals, birds and lizards, also eating fruit and carrion."}, {"id": "marten", "sp": "martes foina", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "A nocturnal mustelid that hunts rodents and birds and also eats fruit."}, {"id": "racer", "sp": "hierophis gemonensis", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "eagle", "sp": "circaetus gallicus", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "raven", "sp": "corvus corax", "xh": 0.9, "wiki": "Common raven", "desc": "An intelligent scavenger that feeds on carrion, including kills left by wolves."}, {"id": "wolf", "sp": "canis lupus", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "A pack hunter of wild ungulates such as chamois, roe deer and boar. It is listed among the large carnivores of the site."}, {"id": "bear", "sp": "ursus arctos", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "Mostly a plant eater, taking acorns, berries and grasses, with meat and carrion in spring. The site is among its last southern European strongholds."}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Summer sun drives growth on the sunny slopes and the high meadows."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "rain & snowmelt", "xh": 0.3, "wiki": "Rain", "desc": "Rain and meltwater feed the woods and meadows, but the limestone drains fast so surface water is scarce."}, {"id": "snow", "sp": "winter snow", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "Snow c